### Phase 3 — Enhanced Prompts: LaTeX/KaTeX + mhchem

#### [MODIFY] [pdf_vision_pipeline.py](file:///d:/ziptrip/projects/nkc-test/backend/ai_preview_importer/pdf_vision_pipeline.py)

Add to both `EXTRACT_PROMPT` and `GENERATE_PROMPT`:

```
CHEMISTRY FORMATTING (mhchem):
- Use \\ce{} for ALL chemical formulas: \\ce{H2O}, \\ce{NaCl}, \\ce{CO2}
- Chemical equations: \\ce{2H2 + O2 -> 2H2O}
- Reversible: \\ce{N2 + 3H2 <=> 2NH3}
- Ions: \\ce{Na+}, \\ce{SO4^{2-}}, \\ce{Fe^{3+}}
- Organic: \\ce{CH3-CH2-OH}, \\ce{C6H12O6}
- State symbols: \\ce{H2O (l)}, \\ce{CO2 (g)}, \\ce{NaCl (aq)}
- Isotopes: \\ce{^{14}C}, \\ce{^{235}U}

IMAGE REFERENCES FOR DIAGRAMS:
- When a question has a diagram, reference it as: ![diagram](DIAGRAM_PAGE_X)
- When an option has a diagram: ![option_diagram](DIAGRAM_PAGE_X_OPT_Y)
- The backend will replace these references with actual image URLs
```

Also update existing LaTeX rules to explicitly use KaTeX-compatible syntax:
- `$...$` for inline math
- `$$...$$` for display math  
- Avoid `\begin{align}` (use `\begin{aligned}` which KaTeX supports)

